  "scope": "GA-v1 first replicates against frozen baseline and reference PSMs; length4, extension0, gaps1, cap50",
  "recommendations": [
    "Retain the current G/A windows and K retention; no evidence-backed additional filter rule.",
    "Report residue-mass consistency as a supplementary metric, not full chemical correctness.",
    "Do not interpret all wrong ordered gap spellings as independent unsupported paths."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "No remaining exact-G/A predicate matches, lowercase endpoints, or modified G/A endpoint near-matches in the scored GA-v1 tables.",
    "All six paper-correct G/A candidate removals are lower-ranked reverse reads with erroneous M oxidation; all fail strict residue-mass scoring.",
    "Wrong M oxidation shifts a reverse R-terminal flank from 174.111676 to158.116761 Da, only .009057 Da from the L-A anchor.",
    "Wider N(.050)/C(.020) tails, N isotope +/-1,+/-2 windows, and their union yield zero posthoc rank1 gains or losses in all9 tables.",
    "All three scored top1 isotope-window candidates have correct monoisotopic precursor masses in independent raw-spectrum checks.",
    "Expanded windows overlap true TA, R and GL prefix masses in the label-free control; the file gate protects this control but mixed labeling remains a concern."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Posthoc replay uses capped outputs and measures rank1 only; no recall or cap-refill claim.",
    "Gap ties use equal reported score/charge and nearly equal rounded flanks; peak paths are not serialized, so identical physical paths are not proven.",
    "The tested variable-modification set contains oxidation of M, not variable G/A modifications.",
    "The detector has one real label-free control and synthetic TMTpro tests; this does not establish general labeling sensitivity or specificity.",
    "Strict correctness still requires only one matching flank; precursor closure and both-flank agreement are not required."
